  "body": "**Blocked by:** #146\n\n## Context\n\nCanonical storage and catalogs exist. All system-label projections must now use them consistently from the authenticated user's locale.\n\n## Task\n\nResolve database names, property names, option labels, view-type names, and agent-tool labels in API response serializers using the authenticated user's `users.locale`; do not accept a locale query/body override. Preserve canonical keys and stable stored values in the response beside display labels where clients need both. Apply the same resolver and locale to runtime-generated AGENT.md permission manifests so the next generation reflects a locale change without persisted manifest edits. Ensure explicit stored overrides win in both API and AGENT.md. Leave user-authored content byte-for-byte unchanged.\n\n## Scope\n\n### In scope\n\n- API and generated-manifest projections plus integration tests for cs/en/fallback/override behavior.\n\n### Out of scope\n\n- Frontend static chrome, locale settings UI, third languages, or translation of user content.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- The same authenticated user receives matching localized labels from API and generated AGENT.md.\n- No request parameter can override `users.locale`; a later locale change affects the next response/generation.\n- Snapshot tests prove user-authored names and content are unchanged and overrides win across locales.\n",
